{"id": "EUVD-2026-108309", "enisaUuid": "d91e274c-b2d1-34f5-b907-e2d36ebae625", "description": "Wasmtime 47.0.0 before 48.0.4 and 49.0.0 before 49.0.2 contains an improper validation vulnerability that accepts components whose core modules import WebAssembly tags with a subtype of the original type. Malicious guests can mis-type exception object payloads to corrupt the GC heap, causing Wasmtime to panic when the exceptions proposal is enabled.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T19:13:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:13:50", "baseScore": 5.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-cfhf-m2cr-62wj", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wasmtime-47.0.0-before-48.0.4-and-49.0.0-before-49.0.2-gc-heap-corruption-via-tag-imports"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cvpp-75f3-xc4p", "CVE-2026-115383"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3854d468-cddd-375f-b21f-d51eb030a152", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "49.0.0 <49.0.2"}, {"id": "c83f65f3-c49b-3da6-a6c4-1fda564c034e", "product": {"name": "wasmtime", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}, "product_version": "47.0.0 <48.0.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ade91b5c-abd0-326f-a5f8-e5ecb5d2f7bd", "vendor": {"name": "bytecodealliance"}}], "isExploited": false}